From: Marionette AirDrop driver research
Subject: [EXPERIMENTAL] stop mission monitor polling before delayed detach

The mission monitor vdev starts dp_mon_vdev_timer for MSI polling. The
rejected 0028 teardown deferred the final datapath delete while that timer
continued to run against a vdev entering logical deletion, and the timer
then faulted. Stop the timer synchronously at the datapath detach entry for
monitor vdevs before any WMA/SME delayed teardown. Existing final delete still
flushes monitor rings; this does not change packet formats or enable TX.

--- a/qca-wifi-host-cmn/dp/wifi3.0/dp_main.c
+++ b/qca-wifi-host-cmn/dp/wifi3.0/dp_main.c
@@ -7483,6 +7483,13 @@
 
 	if (!vdev)
 		return QDF_STATUS_E_FAILURE;
+
+	/* Mission monitor starts a polling timer when the vdev is attached.
+	 * Stop it before any delayed WMA/SME teardown can make the vdev
+	 * unreachable; the normal final-delete path still flushes rings. */
+	if (wlan_op_mode_monitor == vdev->opmode &&
+	    soc->intr_mode == DP_INTR_MSI)
+		dp_monitor_vdev_timer_stop(soc);
 
 	soc->arch_ops.txrx_vdev_detach(soc, vdev);
 
